      "problem": "Given that $\\dfrac {6a} {b^2} = x$ and $\\dfrac {3b} {2a}= y,$ what is $x\\cdot y?$",
      "worked_solution": "We multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot y & =\\frac{6a}{{b}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{3b}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{6a\\cdot 3b}{{b}^{2}\\cdot 2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{18ab}{2a{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In the above example, we performed some cancellations after multiplying. However, with more complex expressions, it's often easier to cancel *before* multiplying.",
